---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "The Circulation Network: four practices, four markets"
description: "Four independent marketing practices working under one set of standards, each owning a single market and a single discipline."
permalink: /network/index.html

hero:
  eyebrow: Four practices, four markets
  title: The Circulation Network
  lede: >-
    The Circulation Network is four independent marketing practices working under
    one set of standards. Each owns a single market and a single discipline:
    search and local search in the United States, dental marketing in the United
    States, design and branding in Peru, and full-service marketing in Mexico.
    Each is staffed by people who live and work in the market it serves.

practicesTitle: The practices
practicesNote: One market, one discipline, each
practices:
  - name: Circulation Studio
    place: Laguna Beach, California
    since: This site
    what: >-
      Search, local search and Yelp advertising for US service businesses.
      Websites built to be found, campaigns measured against booked work rather
      than impressions.
    note: Working with US service businesses since 2011.
    href: /what-we-do/
    label: What we do
    external: false
  - name: Circulation Dental
    place: United States
    since: Founded 2021
    what: >-
      Digital marketing built for dental practices: new patient acquisition,
      treatment-specific campaigns, and the review and referral work a practice
      depends on.
    note: >-
      One discipline, deliberately narrow. A dental practice is a different
      business from a plumbing company, and the marketing is different enough to
      be run by people who only do it.
    href: https://circulationdental.com
    label: circulationdental.com
    external: true
  - name: La Ventana Gris
    place: Lima, Peru
    since: Founded 2021 by Vanessa Pacheco
    what: >-
      Branding, graphic design, interior design and visual merchandising. A design
      practice in the full sense, working from identity through to how a space is
      arranged and how a shelf is set.
    note: Peruvian clients, work made in Lima, and a studio you can walk into.
    href: https://laventanagris.com
    label: laventanagris.com
    sub: Site in Spanish
    external: true
  - name: Elūvia Marketing
    place: San Miguel de Allende, Mexico
    since: Also Queretaro and Mexico City
    what: >-
      Bilingual full-service marketing for the Mexican market, with a focus on
      hospitality, real estate and cultural organisations.
    note: >-
      Campaigns written and run in Spanish and in English by a team living in the
      country, for clients across San Miguel de Allende, Queretaro and Mexico
      City.
    href: https://emkt.mx
    label: emkt.mx
    sub: Site in Spanish and English
    external: true

partnersTitle: Platform partnerships
partnersNote: Held across the network
partnersLede: >-
  Certifications and platform partnerships are held at the network level, so the
  practice doing the work has the access, the training and the support behind it
  regardless of which one you are speaking to.
partners:
  - name: Google Partner
    body: Search and performance campaigns, with Google's partner support behind the account.
  - name: Yelp Advertising Partner
    body: Certified to buy and manage Yelp advertising, with partner tools and client promotions.
  - name: Brizy Partner
    body: The build platform behind client sites, with partner level access and support.
  - name: Shopify Partner
    body: Storefront builds and maintenance for clients selling online.
  - name: UserWay Authorized Affiliate
    body: Accessibility tooling on client sites, licensed rather than bolted on.

why:
  eyebrow: Reference
  title: Why it is structured this way
  body:
    - >-
      Each practice operates where its people live. Local presence, local
      language, local accountability, and a client base in the same market as the
      office. A campaign for a hotel in San Miguel de Allende is written by people
      who eat in that town. Design work made in Lima answers to Peruvian clients
      who can walk into the studio.
    - >-
      All four practices run on Velu, our proprietary agency operating system. It
      holds the standards, the process and the institutional knowledge, which is
      why the work looks the same from Laguna Beach as it does from Lima.
  muted: >-
    Each practice has its own clients, its own leadership and its own market to
    answer to. That is why the work is good: a studio that has to keep its own
    city happy gets better at its discipline than a department that only has to
    keep another office happy.
  holdTitle: What holds them together
  holds:
    - One standard for how work is scoped, measured and reported.
    - Shared people, in the places where two disciplines meet.
    - One founder accountable across all four, and one place a client escalation lands.

means:
  title: What this means for a Circulation Studio client
  lede: Three things you can ask for, on the day you need them.
  items:
    - name: Design capacity when a project needs it
      body: >-
        A brand system, a print piece or an environment is work a design practice
        does better than a search agency. When a project calls for it, we say so
        and bring it in.
    - name: Creative direction beyond the campaign
      body: >-
        A second set of eyes on identity and art direction, from people who spend
        all day on it rather than between reporting cycles.
    - name: Reach into two more markets
      body: >-
        If your business needs to speak to a Mexican or Peruvian audience, there
        is a team in that country to write it, place it and answer the phone.

pages:
  eyebrow: Also in the network, not a practice
  name: Elūvia Pages
  kicker: A product, not an agency
  body: >-
    Mobile-first swipeable microsites for campaigns and promotions. Built to be
    handed to a phone, not browsed on a desktop.
  href: https://eluvia.page
  label: eluvia.page
---
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}

{#
  THE CIRCULATION NETWORK, at /network/. FOOTER NAVIGATION ONLY.

  It is reference rather than a service page: someone who wants to know what the
  other practices are, or who found one of them and is working out how they
  relate. Putting it in the main nav would spend a top-level slot on something
  almost nobody arrives looking for. nav.js carries it in `footer` only.

  CIRCULATION STUDIO IS LAGUNA BEACH. Elūvia Marketing is the practice in San
  Miguel de Allende, and saying so here is the opposite of the bleed-over
  CLAUDE.md bans: that rule exists because earlier docs described THIS studio as
  Mexico-based. Naming a different practice's real market is what makes the two
  distinguishable, which is the whole point of the page.

  ENGLISH ONLY. The two "Site in Spanish" labels describe what a reader will
  find if they follow the link, in English. Nothing here is a Spanish mirror,
  and there is no language switcher.

  ONE INK PANE, and no madder pane at all. The "why" section is the deep one.
#}

{% call container(class="cs-net-crumbs") %}
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol class="cs-net-crumbs__list">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">The Circulation Network</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>
{% endcall %}

{#- 1 HERO -#}
{% call container(class="cs-net-section cs-net-section--first") %}
  <p class="cs-eyebrow">{{ hero.eyebrow }}</p>
  <h1 class="cs-net-hero__title">{{ hero.title }}</h1>
  <p class="cs-net-hero__lede">{{ hero.lede }}</p>
{% endcall %}

{#- 2 THE FOUR PRACTICES -#}
{% call container(class="cs-net-section") %}
  <div class="cs-net-head cs-net-head--strong">
    <h2 class="cs-net-h2">{{ practicesTitle }}</h2>
    <p class="cs-net-meta">{{ practicesNote }}</p>
  </div>
  {%- for p in practices %}
  <div class="cs-net-band">
    <div>
      <p class="cs-net-band__name">{{ p.name }}</p>
      <p class="cs-net-band__place">{{ p.place }}</p>
      <p class="cs-net-band__since">{{ p.since }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-net-band__what">
      <p class="cs-net-band__lede">{{ p.what }}</p>
      <p class="cs-net-band__note">{{ p.note }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-net-band__go">
      <a href="{{ p.href }}"{% if p.external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>
        {{ p.label }}
        {%- if p.external %}
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 5H6a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v12a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-5"></path><path d="M13 11l8-8"></path><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path></svg>
        <span class="sr-only">Opens in a new tab</span>
        {%- else %}<span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>{% endif %}
      </a>
      {%- if p.sub %}<span class="cs-net-band__sub">{{ p.sub }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endfor %}
{% endcall %}

{#- 2b PLATFORM PARTNERSHIPS -#}
{% call container(class="cs-net-section") %}
  <div class="cs-net-head">
    <h2 class="cs-net-h2">{{ partnersTitle }}</h2>
    <p class="cs-net-meta">{{ partnersNote }}</p>
  </div>
  <p class="cs-net-lede">{{ partnersLede }}</p>
  <div class="cs-net-partners">
    {%- for p in partners %}
    <div class="cs-net-partners__item">
      <p class="cs-net-partners__name">{{ p.name }}</p>
      <p class="cs-net-partners__body">{{ p.body }}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{#- 3 WHY, THE ONE INK PANE. Full bleed, so it is the only band that leaves
    the container. -#}
<div class="cs-net-why">
  {% call container(class="cs-net-why__inner") %}
    <p class="cs-net-why__eyebrow">{{ why.eyebrow }}</p>
    <h2 class="cs-net-why__title">{{ why.title }}</h2>
    <div class="cs-net-why__grid">
      <div>
        {%- for p in why.body %}<p class="cs-net-why__body">{{ p }}</p>{% endfor %}
        <p class="cs-net-why__muted">{{ why.muted }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-net-why__hold">
        <p class="cs-net-why__hold-title">{{ why.holdTitle }}</p>
        <ul>
          {%- for h in why.holds %}<li>{{ h }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{#- 4 WHAT THIS MEANS -#}
{% call container(class="cs-net-section") %}
  <div class="cs-net-head cs-net-head--stack">
    <h2 class="cs-net-h2">{{ means.title }}</h2>
    <p class="cs-net-lede cs-net-lede--tight">{{ means.lede }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cs-net-means">
    {%- for item in means.items %}
    <div class="cs-net-means__item">
      <p class="cs-net-means__name">{{ item.name }}</p>
      <p class="cs-net-means__body">{{ item.body }}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{#- 5 ELUVIA PAGES -#}
{% call container(class="cs-net-section") %}
  <p class="cs-eyebrow cs-net-pages__eyebrow">{{ pages.eyebrow }}</p>
  <div class="cs-net-pages">
    <div>
      <p class="cs-net-pages__name">{{ pages.name }}</p>
      <p class="cs-net-pages__kicker">{{ pages.kicker }}</p>
    </div>
    <p class="cs-net-pages__body">{{ pages.body }}</p>
    <a class="cs-net-pages__go" href="{{ pages.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      {{ pages.label }}
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 5H6a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v12a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-5"></path><path d="M13 11l8-8"></path><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path></svg>
      <span class="sr-only">Opens in a new tab</span>
    </a>
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{#- SCHEMA. FOUR SIBLING ORGANIZATIONS AND ONE PERSON. NO HIERARCHY.

    Deliberately no parentOrganization and no subOrganization. Those assert a
    corporate structure that has not been confirmed, and schema is not the place
    to guess at one: an ownership claim in structured data is a claim, and
    unpicking it after a search engine has resolved the entities against it is
    far harder than adding it later.

    So each practice is its own Organization identified by its own site through
    sameAs, and the founder is one Person with sameAs including stevelepore.me.
    What relates them on this page is the prose, which is accurate, rather than
    a graph edge that would be an invention. -#}
{%- set orgs = [] -%}
{%- for p in practices -%}
  {%- set _ = orgs.push({
    "@type": "Organization",
    "@id": (page.url | absoluteUrl) + "#" + (p.name | lower | replace(" ", "-") | replace("ū", "u")),
    "name": p.name,
    "description": p.what,
    "areaServed": p.place,
    "sameAs": [ p.external and p.href or site.url + "/" ]
  }) -%}
{%- endfor %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{{ {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": orgs.concat([{
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": (page.url | absoluteUrl) + "#founder",
    "name": authors.steve.name,
    "jobTitle": authors.steve.role,
    "sameAs": ["https://stevelepore.me"]
  }])
} | jsonld | safe }}
</script>
